## Summary

The bug was in `submit_user_message_with_history_and_shell_escape_policy` in `codex-rs/tui/src/chatwidget.rs`.

When building the `Op::UserTurn` operation on message submission, the code had a special-case that forced the permission profile to `None` whenever the session's sandbox policy was the external sandbox variant:

```rust
let permission_profile = if matches!(
    self.config.permissions.sandbox_policy.get(),
    SandboxPolicy::ExternalSandbox { .. }
) {
    None
} else {
    Some(self.config.permissions.permission_profile())
};
```

This dropped the configured permission profile precisely for `SandboxPolicy::ExternalSandbox`, while every other sandbox variant preserved it. I replaced it with an unconditional pass-through:

```rust
let permission_profile = Some(self.config.permissions.permission_profile());
```

Now the permission profile from the session configuration is always included in the submitted user turn, regardless of the active sandbox policy variant — including the legacy external sandbox variant. `config.permissions.permission_profile()` already maps an external sandbox to the correct `PermissionProfile::External { network }`, so the profile is preserved rather than nulled out. `SandboxPolicy` remains imported and used elsewhere in the file, so no unused-import warnings, and the `codex-tui` crate type-checks.
